course: dictionary
lesson: 1880
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning. A dictionary lists them as 1), 2), 3) and so on. To find the right one, read the words around it. «Coins thrown into a wishing fountain are usually collected for charity.» Here collect means to ask people for money and get it, because charity and coins are the clues.
explain: Collect can also mean to gather things together in one place. «Collect conkers, acorns and pine cones for crafts.» Nobody is asking for money here. The clue is the things you pick up and keep.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence to check it. In «Scientists use drones to count whales and even to collect whale breath», collect means gather or take in something hard to catch. "Gather" still makes sense in the sentence, so you have found the right meaning.
explain: Collect can mean to go and pick someone up, as in «The children collect shells on the beach.» Look at the words around collect, not just the word itself. Then you will know which meaning the writer chose.
fact: Collect is a verb: collect, collects, collected, collecting.
fact: «Collect» means to gather things together into one place.
fact: «Collect» can mean to keep many things of one kind as a hobby, like stamps, shells or cards.
fact: «Collect» can mean to go and pick someone up, or to ask people for money for a charity.
fact: In science, you can collect data, which means gathering information so that you can study it.
exercise: «Coins thrown into a wishing fountain are usually collected for charity.» What does collected mean here? | Counted by a robot | *Gathered by asking people for money | Hidden under the stones | Thrown away into the water
exercise: «Collect conkers, acorns and pine cones for crafts, but never eat conkers or acorns.» What should you never do with conkers or acorns? | Collect them | *Eat them | Use them for crafts | Keep them in a box
exercise: What does «collect» mean when someone says they collect stamps as a hobby? | *Keeps many stamps of one kind | Sends letters to a friend | Throws the stamps in the bin | Cuts the stamps into shapes
test: Which sentence uses collect to mean go and pick someone up? | The bins are emptied every Monday | The bees collect nectar from the flowers | *Dad will collect me from football at six | The baker will collect bread for the shop
test: In «Scientists collect data about the weather», what does collect mean? | *Gather and record | Drop on the floor | Throw away | Buy in a shop
exam: Read «The kite collected electric charge from storm clouds.» Which meaning fits best? | *Gathered in from the storm clouds | Painted onto a sheet of paper | Sent back to the ground in a letter | Thrown out into the sky
